            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, Congress enacted the Indian Reorganization Act of 1934, authorizing the Secretary of the Interior to take land in trust for Indians and using the phrase \u201cmembers of any recognized Indian tribe now under Federal jurisdiction.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justices",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "890bdffb96a26d674981622614d43b1f52f4864aa0a4b60b2af7d1450500cbb0",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0002",
              "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0003",
              "ev-890bdffb96a2-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 13,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The justices asked how to give meaning to the word \u201cnow,\u201d questioning whether it should be read as referring to the time of enactment (\u201cthen\u201d) or to the present (\u201cnow\u201d)."
      }
    ],
